            <ArticleTitle>[Prevention of stress and hypoxic damage to the heart using the beta-blockader inderal].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>90-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Administration of the beta-blocker Inderal, 1 mg/kg, prior to emotional-painful stress was shown to prevent post-stress damage of contractility in isolated rat hearts. Inderal enhances animal heart resistance to hypoxic and reoxygenation damage and prevents progress thereof after the stress.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
